[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: Addressed pret_cov.transition_frequency_starvation coverage for every facet that the pretense authoring contract permits tests to exercise, adding seven real-implementation scenario tests: (1) empty-graph analysis - validate, topological_sort [], find_roots/leaves empty, compute_critical_path(None) == ([], 0.0), next_wave [], get_all_states {}, is_finished True; (2) deferred dependency checks - add_node with an absent dependency registers alpha without eager rejection, has_node false for the phantom, get_dependencies {'phantom'}, roots empty, leaves {alpha}, no ready wave; (3) removal of an interior node purges incident edges in both directions and the scheduler record (get_all_states drops the removed identifier, alpha stays READY); (4) is_finished while a node is RUNNING returns False and after a failure blocks a later-added dependent returns True with an empty ready wave; (5) mark_failed CONTINUE_ON_ERROR skips the dependent, retains the independent READY node, reports unfinished, then runs it to completion; (6) skip-downstream over a diamond graph marks the shared dependent SKIPPED exactly once (transitive dedup). Remaining facets in the report are checked *Error preconditions (DuplicateNodeError, NodeNotFoundError for add_edge/remove_node/get_node/get_state endpoints, CycleError for validate/topological_sort); guides/pretense.md gates these in the interface state machine via require/require_arg and states preconditions cannot be tested and asserting *Error exceptions is strictly prohibited, so their rejection paths are intentionally left unasserted rather than violated by tests.
